"""Essays with separate arguments, examples and conclusions for each brief."""
from exam_common import case, p, coverage as c
G='writing-task2'
def samples():
    return [
case(G,'coeducation','Học chung nam nữ: ưu và nhược điểm','Strengths and weaknesses of mixed-gender education','advantages','Ưu điểm và nhược điểm',
    'Examine the strengths and weaknesses of educating boys and girls together. Support your discussion with reasons and examples. Write at least 250 words.',
    ['Phân tích cả ưu điểm lẫn nhược điểm của việc học chung.', 'Ví dụ phải liên quan đến lớp học nam nữ, không chỉ giáo dục nói chung.', 'Không đổi đề thành chỉ so sánh trường công và trường tư.'],[
        p('Đặt vấn đề','In many schools, boys and girls study in the same classrooms and take part in the same activities. This arrangement can prepare children for everyday life, but it also creates challenges that teachers need to manage. The main strengths of mixed education concern cooperation and equal opportunities, while its weaknesses may include social pressure and unequal participation.', 'Giới thiệu đúng hai mặt sẽ phân tích.'),
        p('Ưu điểm có cơ chế và ví dụ','One important advantage is that students learn to work with people of another gender from an early age. For example, a mixed science project requires classmates to share equipment, discuss ideas and divide tasks. These experiences can make cooperation at university or work feel more natural later. Mixed schools can also challenge narrow ideas about what boys or girls should do. When a girl leads a robotics group or a boy performs well in literature, classmates can judge ability through real achievements rather than assumptions.', 'Không khẳng định mọi lớp học chung đều bình đẳng; giải thích cơ hội tạo ra.'),
        p('Nhược điểm cụ thể','However, simply putting students together does not guarantee a comfortable learning environment. Some teenagers may avoid asking questions because they worry about being judged by classmates. Unequal expectations can also continue inside a mixed classroom. A teacher might, without intending to, ask boys to handle equipment and girls to take notes. If this happens repeatedly, students have fewer chances to develop different skills. Schools therefore need clear rules against teasing and should rotate responsibilities during group work instead of allowing the same children to lead every activity.', 'Nhược điểm có tình huống cụ thể; giải pháp chỉ hỗ trợ phân tích.'),
        p('Tổng hợp','In conclusion, educating boys and girls together offers useful preparation for social and working life and can widen opportunities. Nevertheless, social pressure and unfair classroom habits can limit these benefits. Its success depends on how teachers organise participation and respond when students feel excluded.', 'Tổng hợp cả hai mặt; không kết luận tuyệt đối.')],
    [('equal opportunities','cơ hội bình đẳng'),('social pressure','áp lực xã hội'),('rotate responsibilities','luân phiên trách nhiệm')],source='dthu',page=18,
    checks=[c('Ưu điểm','learn to work with people of another gender'),c('Ví dụ','mixed science project'),c('Nhược điểm','avoid asking questions'),c('Kết luận cân bằng','can limit these benefits')]),
case(G,'tourism-communities','Du lịch tác động đến cộng đồng địa phương','Positive and negative effects on residents','effects','Tác động tích cực và tiêu cực',
    'Discuss how tourism affects local communities, considering favourable and unfavourable effects. Develop your points with reasons and examples. Write at least 250 words.',
    ['Đối tượng trọng tâm là người dân và cộng đồng tại nơi đón khách.', 'Phân tích mặt tích cực và tiêu cực, mỗi mặt có ví dụ.', 'Không dành thân bài để kể lợi ích đi du lịch đối với bản thân du khách.'],[
        p('Xác định đối tượng','Tourism brings visitors into contact with places where other people live and work. For local communities, this can create valuable income and support public services. At the same time, a large number of visitors can put pressure on housing and the environment. Both effects deserve attention when a town decides how to develop its tourism industry.', 'Trọng tâm là cộng đồng đón khách.'),
        p('Tác động tích cực','On the positive side, visitor spending can support a range of local jobs. A family that opens a small guesthouse may buy vegetables from nearby farmers, hire a cleaner and recommend local guides. Money therefore reaches more people than just the owner of a hotel. Tourism can also give residents a reason to maintain traditional buildings or crafts. For example, income from guided visits to an old village could help pay for repairs, allowing both visitors and future generations of residents to enjoy it.', 'Nêu dòng tiền đến nhiều nhóm cư dân; ví dụ được đặt giả định bằng could.'),
        p('Tác động tiêu cực','However, the benefits are not shared equally, and rapid growth can make daily life harder. If landlords convert ordinary flats into short-term accommodation, residents may struggle to find affordable homes. Busy streets, late-night noise and litter can also reduce the quality of life in a popular neighbourhood. A coastal community, for instance, may earn more from restaurants while facing extra rubbish on the beach. If public services do not grow with visitor numbers, local people have to deal with these problems throughout the holiday season.', 'Không chỉ nói ô nhiễm chung; liên hệ nhà ở và sinh hoạt cư dân.'),
        p('Kết luận','In conclusion, tourism can provide employment and protect local heritage, but it can also increase living pressures and damage shared spaces. Development should therefore involve residents in decisions about housing, waste collection and visitor activities. A successful destination should remain a good place to live as well as an attractive place to visit.', 'Ý kiến quản lý ngắn ở kết; không tự đổi thành bài nguyên nhân–giải pháp.')],
    [('local communities','cộng đồng địa phương'),('affordable homes','nhà ở có giá phù hợp'),('local heritage','di sản địa phương')],source='ufls',page=15,
    checks=[c('Mặt tích cực cho cư dân','support a range of local jobs'),c('Mặt tiêu cực','struggle to find affordable homes'),c('Ví dụ gắn cộng đồng','coastal community')]),
case(G,'school-phones','Có nên cấm hoàn toàn điện thoại ở trường?','A qualified position on school phone rules','opinion-partial','Quan điểm có giới hạn',
    'Some people believe secondary schools should ban students from bringing mobile phones onto school grounds. To what extent do you agree or disagree? Explain your position with reasons and examples. Write at least 250 words.',
    ['Phân biệt cấm mang đến trường với cấm dùng trong giờ.', 'Lập trường nhất quán: phản đối lệnh cấm hoàn toàn, ủng hộ quản lý giờ dùng.', 'Hai lý do chính phải hỗ trợ lập trường này.'],[
        p('Lập trường rõ','Mobile phones can interrupt lessons, so it is understandable that some people want them removed from schools. However, I disagree with a complete ban on bringing them onto school grounds. Schools should control when phones are used, but students may still need them for travel arrangements and carefully planned learning activities. These needs are different from using a phone freely during class.', 'Không đánh tráo cấm mang với hạn chế sử dụng.'),
        p('Lý do về liên lạc','First, many secondary students travel to school without their parents. A phone allows a child to contact home if a bus is cancelled or an after-school activity finishes early. For example, a student who normally walks home with a friend may need to arrange a different way home when that friend is absent. School offices can help with emergencies, but they may not always be open when clubs finish. Allowing a switched-off phone in a bag gives families a practical way to deal with these changes.', 'Ví dụ về thay đổi lịch trình, không phóng đại thành mọi tình huống nguy hiểm.'),
        p('Học tập và xử lý phản biện','Phones can also support limited classroom tasks when a teacher gives permission. Students might record a short pronunciation exercise and listen to it again to notice mistakes. This does not mean that they should check messages during explanations. Notifications and games can distract both the owner and nearby classmates, so a clear rule is necessary: phones stay silent and out of sight unless the teacher asks students to use them. Repeated misuse could lead to the phone being kept safely in the school office until the end of the day.', 'Thừa nhận xao nhãng và giới hạn cách dùng.'),
        p('Kết luận nhất quán','In conclusion, I support strict limits on phone use during lessons, but not a ban on bringing phones to school. A controlled approach protects learning time while recognising students’ practical communication needs. The rule should explain when use is allowed and what happens when students ignore it.', 'Giữ nguyên mức độ phản đối đã nêu ở mở bài.')],
    [('school grounds','khuôn viên trường'),('out of sight','ngoài tầm nhìn'),('practical communication needs','nhu cầu liên lạc thực tế')],
    checks=[c('Lập trường','disagree with a complete ban'),c('Lý do 1','travel to school without their parents'),c('Lý do 2','support limited classroom tasks'),c('Thừa nhận mặt trái','Notifications and games can distract')]),
case(G,'online-campus','Học đại học trực tuyến hay tại trường?','Access versus face-to-face learning','discussion','Bàn hai quan điểm và ý kiến riêng',
    'Some people think universities should offer most courses online to widen access. Others believe students learn better by attending classes on campus. Discuss both views and give your own opinion. Write at least 250 words.',
    ['Giải thích vì sao mỗi phía có lý, không chỉ kể hai lựa chọn.', 'Nêu ý kiến riêng và phạm vi áp dụng.', 'Liên hệ hình thức học với nhu cầu sinh viên và môn học.'],[
        p('Hai quan điểm','Universities can now teach students without requiring them to be in the same room. Supporters of online courses see this as a way to widen access, while others value learning on campus. Both views address real needs. In my opinion, universities should offer online access to suitable content while keeping regular opportunities for practical work and direct discussion.', 'Nêu giải pháp kết hợp và giới hạn ngay đầu.'),
        p('Lý do của phía trực tuyến','On the one hand, online courses can help people whose circumstances make daily attendance difficult. A student living far from a city may avoid the cost of renting a room near university. Recorded lectures can also be useful to someone who works shifts, because the material can be studied at another time. For example, a working parent might watch a lecture after putting a child to bed and submit questions before a scheduled discussion. Without this flexibility, that person might have to delay further study altogether.', 'Giải thích access bằng chi phí, nơi ở và thời gian.'),
        p('Lý do của phía tại trường','On the other hand, attending classes provides structure and easier contact with teachers and classmates. A student who is confused can ask for an explanation immediately, and group activities are less dependent on a reliable internet connection. Some subjects also require equipment that students cannot reasonably keep at home. A nursing student, for instance, needs supervised practice rather than only watching demonstrations on a screen. Campus study can therefore be particularly valuable for courses where feedback, teamwork and physical practice are central to learning.', 'Không đánh đồng mọi môn; lấy ví dụ cần thực hành.'),
        p('Ý kiến và kết','In conclusion, online learning makes university more accessible, while campus teaching supports interaction and practical skills. I favour combining the two according to the course: lectures could be available online, with scheduled seminars, laboratories or placements in person. This would widen participation without assuming that every learning task can be completed equally well from home.', 'Quan điểm riêng có cách áp dụng cụ thể.')],
    [('widen access','mở rộng khả năng tiếp cận'),('works shifts','làm việc theo ca'),('supervised practice','thực hành có người hướng dẫn')],
    checks=[c('Phía 1','avoid the cost of renting'),c('Phía 2','provides structure'),c('Ý kiến riêng','I favour combining the two')]),
case(G,'traffic-causes','Ùn tắc giờ cao điểm: nguyên nhân và giải pháp','Private vehicles and unreliable public transport','cause-solution','Nguyên nhân và giải pháp',
    'Traffic congestion during rush hour is a growing problem in many cities. Why does it happen, and what can local authorities do to reduce it? Give reasons and relevant examples. Write at least 250 words.',
    ['Giải thích nguyên nhân ùn tắc, không chỉ tác hại.', 'Giải pháp do chính quyền địa phương thực hiện.', 'Mỗi giải pháp phải xử lý một nguyên nhân đã nêu.'],[
        p('Nêu vấn đề','Traffic congestion makes daily travel slow and unpredictable in many cities. Although busy roads are often blamed on individual drivers, the problem is also connected with the choices available to commuters and the timing of everyday activities. Heavy dependence on private vehicles and concentrated travel times are two important causes that local authorities can address through transport planning.', 'Hai nguyên nhân dẫn đường cho thân bài.'),
        p('Nguyên nhân thứ nhất và giải pháp','The first cause is that public transport may not be a practical alternative. If buses are infrequent, crowded or far from residential areas, people are more likely to drive even for journeys they make every day. For example, a worker who must change buses twice may choose a motorbike to avoid arriving late. Local authorities could improve routes connecting homes with major workplaces and give buses priority at busy junctions. Frequent, dependable services would make leaving a private vehicle at home a more realistic choice.', 'Xe cá nhân nhiều → xe buýt đáng tin cậy hơn; không chỉ hô hào.'),
        p('Nguyên nhân thứ hai và giải pháp','Another reason is that schools and offices often begin at similar times, concentrating many journeys into a short period. Roads near school gates can become especially crowded when parents stop to drop off children. Councils could work with schools and large employers to stagger starting times where possible. They could also create safe walking routes and organised drop-off areas away from the busiest junctions. These measures would not remove every vehicle, but they could spread demand and prevent a small blockage from delaying an entire street.', 'Giải pháp đúng thẩm quyền phối hợp của địa phương.'),
        p('Kết luận','In conclusion, rush-hour congestion is linked to weak alternatives to private transport and too many journeys taking place at once. Improving bus services and coordinating travel times would tackle these causes directly. Building more roads alone is unlikely to be enough if the same patterns of vehicle use remain unchanged.', 'Tóm tắt cặp nguyên nhân–giải pháp; không thêm nguyên nhân mới.')],
    [('rush hour','giờ cao điểm'),('public transport','giao thông công cộng'),('stagger starting times','bố trí giờ bắt đầu lệch nhau')],
    checks=[c('Nguyên nhân 1','buses are infrequent'),c('Giải pháp 1','improve routes'),c('Nguyên nhân 2','begin at similar times'),c('Giải pháp 2','stagger starting times')]),
case(G,'rural-migration','Người trẻ rời quê lên thành phố','Reasons for migration and effects on rural communities','cause-effect','Nguyên nhân và hệ quả',
    'Many young adults leave rural areas to live in cities. What are the main reasons for this movement, and how does it affect the rural communities they leave behind? Write an essay of at least 250 words with examples.',
    ['Nêu lý do người trẻ chuyển đi.', 'Phần hệ quả tập trung vùng quê họ rời đi.', 'Không thay nửa bài bằng giải pháp phát triển thành phố.'],[
        p('Giới thiệu','Moving to a city is an important decision for many young adults from rural areas. They often hope to study, find steady work or build a more independent life. While this movement can benefit individuals, it also changes the communities they leave behind. The main reasons concern education and employment, and the effects include both financial support and a loss of local workers.', 'Xác định đúng nơi chịu tác động theo đề.'),
        p('Nguyên nhân','One major reason is that universities and specialised training centres are often located in cities. A school leaver who wants to become an engineer may have few suitable courses close to home. Employment opportunities also influence the decision. Farming income can vary with the season, whereas a factory or office job may offer a more regular wage. Young people may therefore see moving as a way to support themselves and their families. Having friends or relatives already living in the city can make the move feel less uncertain.', 'Hai nguyên nhân thực chất: học và việc làm.'),
        p('Hệ quả ở quê','For rural communities, the effects are mixed. Money sent home can help parents pay bills, improve a house or keep younger children in school. A young worker might also return with useful skills and savings to start a business. However, when many people of working age leave, farms and local services may struggle to find staff. Older residents may have to manage physically demanding tasks without nearby family support. Shops can lose customers as well, making it harder for small businesses to survive throughout the year.', 'Cả tích cực lẫn tiêu cực đều hướng về cộng đồng quê nhà.'),
        p('Kết luận','In conclusion, young adults are mainly attracted by educational opportunities and more reliable employment. Their departure can bring money and new knowledge back to rural areas, but it may also weaken the local workforce and everyday support networks. The overall effect depends partly on whether migrants maintain connections with home and eventually invest their skills there.', 'Không tự chuyển thành bài đề xuất chính sách.')],
    [('steady work','công việc ổn định'),('money sent home','tiền gửi về quê'),('local workforce','lực lượng lao động địa phương')],
    checks=[c('Nguyên nhân học tập','specialised training centres'),c('Nguyên nhân việc làm','a more regular wage'),c('Hệ quả tốt ở quê','Money sent home'),c('Hệ quả xấu ở quê','struggle to find staff')]),
case(G,'plastic-deliveries','Rác bao bì từ đồ ăn giao tận nhà','Problems caused by packaging and matching solutions','problem-solution','Vấn đề và giải pháp',
    'Food delivery services often use large amounts of disposable packaging. What problems does this create, and what could businesses and customers do to reduce them? Write at least 250 words, supporting your ideas with examples.',
    ['Phân tích vấn đề do bao bì dùng một lần gây ra.', 'Có hành động của cả doanh nghiệp lẫn người mua.', 'Không dành thân bài kể nguyên nhân người ta đặt đồ ăn.'],[
        p('Nêu vấn đề','Ordering food at home is convenient, but a single meal can arrive with several containers, bags and plastic utensils. When this happens across a city every day, the amount of disposable packaging becomes a serious practical problem. It increases the burden on waste collection and can pollute shared spaces. Businesses and customers both have ways to reduce unnecessary packaging.', 'Không chuyển sang ưu nhược điểm của việc đặt đồ ăn.'),
        p('Tác hại','One problem is that takeaway packaging is not always easy to recycle. Containers covered in oil or sauce may need special cleaning, and several different materials can be used in the same order. This makes sorting more difficult for households and waste workers. Packaging that is not collected properly can also block drains or end up in rivers. For example, a thin plastic bag dropped near a street drain may be carried away during heavy rain, turning a small piece of litter into a problem beyond the customer’s neighbourhood.', 'Tác hại có chuỗi giải thích, tránh khẳng định tất cả bao bì đều tái chế được.'),
        p('Giải pháp hai phía','Businesses could start by making disposable cutlery optional instead of adding it automatically. A customer eating at home usually has a spoon already. Restaurants could also use fewer separate containers when food can safely be packed together. Where reliable washing and collection are available, a deposit system for reusable boxes may work for regular local customers. Customers, meanwhile, can refuse items they do not need, choose suitable collection options and follow local sorting instructions. Returning reusable containers promptly would help a deposit scheme continue operating.', 'Cả doanh nghiệp và khách; giải pháp hộp tái dùng có điều kiện vệ sinh.'),
        p('Kết luận','In conclusion, disposable food packaging creates difficulties for waste systems and can damage the local environment. Reducing unnecessary items should come before relying on recycling alone. Businesses can change how orders are packed, while customers can support these changes through small, repeatable choices each time they order a meal.', 'Tổng hợp đúng vấn đề–giải pháp.')],
    [('disposable packaging','bao bì dùng một lần'),('plastic utensils','dụng cụ ăn bằng nhựa'),('deposit system','hệ thống đặt cọc')],
    checks=[c('Vấn đề xử lý rác','not always easy to recycle'),c('Vấn đề môi trường','block drains'),c('Doanh nghiệp','making disposable cutlery optional'),c('Khách hàng','refuse items they do not need')]),
case(G,'gap-year','Nghỉ một năm trước đại học: lợi có lớn hơn hại?','Weighing experience against cost and lost study habits','outweigh','So sánh sức nặng lợi và hại',
    'Some school leavers take a year to work or travel before entering university. Do the advantages of taking a gap year outweigh the disadvantages? Give a clear judgement and support it with reasons and examples. Write at least 250 words.',
    ['Nêu bên nào có sức nặng hơn, không chỉ liệt kê.', 'Thừa nhận bất lợi thật sự trước khi cân nhắc.', 'Nếu kết luận có điều kiện, giữ điều kiện nhất quán.'],[
        p('Đánh giá tổng thể','A gap year gives school leavers time to work or travel before starting university. It can delay formal study and create financial difficulties, but it can also help young people make better decisions about their future. In my view, the advantages outweigh the disadvantages when the year has a realistic purpose and does not require the student to take on substantial debt.', 'Đưa đánh giá và điều kiện, không nói mọi gap year đều tốt.'),
        p('Cân nhắc bất lợi','The disadvantages should be taken seriously. A year of travel may be expensive, especially for a family already saving for tuition fees. Students may also find it difficult to return to regular study after a long break. For example, someone who has stopped practising mathematics could struggle during the first weeks of an engineering course. These costs are meaningful because the student still needs to complete a degree later. A gap year without a plan may therefore add stress rather than provide useful preparation.', 'Nêu tác hại cụ thể trước khi đánh giá.'),
        p('Vì sao lợi có thể lớn hơn','Nevertheless, a planned year of work can have a lasting benefit: it may help a student choose a suitable degree. Working as an assistant in a hotel, for instance, could reveal whether someone enjoys dealing with guests before committing to a tourism course. This experience may prevent a costly change of direction after enrolment. Paid work can also build savings and teach punctuality, budgeting and responsibility. These skills remain useful throughout university, whereas some disadvantages can be limited by choosing affordable activities and keeping a weekly study routine.', 'So sánh độ bền của lợi ích và cách giảm hại, không đếm số ý.'),
        p('Kết luận','In conclusion, I believe a purposeful, affordable gap year offers more benefits than drawbacks. Better career decisions and practical skills can influence several years of later study and work. However, if the plan involves heavy borrowing or no clear activity, the balance may change, and starting university immediately could be the wiser choice.', 'Kết luận giữ nguyên điều kiện ở mở bài.')],
    [('take on debt','gánh khoản nợ'),('tuition fees','học phí'),('a weekly study routine','thói quen học hằng tuần')],
    checks=[c('Đánh giá','advantages outweigh the disadvantages'),c('Bất lợi','find it difficult to return'),c('So sánh trọng lượng','These skills remain useful'),c('Điều kiện','purposeful, affordable gap year')]),
case(G,'public-libraries','Internet có khiến thư viện công cộng hết cần thiết?','Public access, study space and help with information','opinion-disagree','Phản đối một nhận định',
    'Because information is available online, some people say local governments should stop funding public libraries. Do you agree or disagree? Give reasons and relevant examples. Write at least 250 words.',
    ['Trả lời việc ngừng cấp ngân sách, không chỉ nói thích sách giấy.', 'Nêu vai trò thư viện khi đã có internet.', 'Thừa nhận cần thay đổi dịch vụ nhưng giữ lập trường rõ.'],[
        p('Lập trường','The internet allows people to find information quickly, so it is reasonable to ask how public libraries should change. However, I disagree with the suggestion that local governments should stop funding them. Libraries provide access, space and guidance that an internet connection alone cannot guarantee. Their services may need updating, but this is a reason to improve public funding decisions rather than remove support entirely.', 'Phản đối ngừng tài trợ, không phản đối internet.'),
        p('Tiếp cận và nơi học','First, information being online does not mean everyone can use it comfortably. Some residents share a phone with family members or cannot afford a reliable computer. A public library can provide equipment and a quiet place to complete important tasks. For example, a person applying for work may need to prepare a document, upload it and check several job descriptions. Doing all of this on a small phone in a crowded home can be difficult. Library computers and study tables make the same opportunity more accessible.', 'Một nhu cầu cụ thể chứng minh vai trò công cộng.'),
        p('Hướng dẫn và sử dụng ngân sách','Libraries can also help people use information more effectively. A librarian can show a learner how to locate an appropriate reference book or compare sources, rather than simply accept the first search result. Libraries may organise reading activities for children whose parents have limited time or money for books. Of course, not every existing service deserves to remain unchanged. Local governments should examine attendance, listen to residents and support a mixture of useful print and digital resources. This would make spending more responsive to actual needs.', 'Thừa nhận vấn đề chi tiêu không đồng nghĩa đồng ý đóng cửa.'),
        p('Kết luận','In conclusion, online information has changed the role of libraries but has not removed their value. Public support should continue because residents still need fair access to equipment, suitable study spaces and help finding reliable material. Updating library services is a more useful response than assuming the internet serves everyone equally well.', 'Kết nối ba vai trò đã lập luận.')],
    [('public funding','nguồn tài trợ công'),('reliable computer','máy tính hoạt động đáng tin cậy'),('compare sources','so sánh các nguồn thông tin')],
    checks=[c('Phản đối dừng ngân sách','stop funding them'),c('Lý do tiếp cận','cannot afford a reliable computer'),c('Lý do hướng dẫn','compare sources'),c('Kết luận','Public support should continue')]),
case(G,'exercise-time','Vì sao ít vận động và làm sao thay đổi?','Barriers for working adults and realistic daily habits','two-questions','Hai câu hỏi kết hợp',
    'Many working adults know exercise is useful but do little physical activity. What makes regular exercise difficult for them? What changes could they make to fit more activity into daily life? Write at least 250 words with examples.',
    ['Đối tượng là người lớn đi làm.', 'Trả lời khó khăn và thay đổi do chính họ thực hiện.', 'Gợi ý khả thi với lịch làm việc; không thay bằng chính sách nhà nước.'],[
        p('Giới thiệu hai câu hỏi','Knowing that exercise is useful does not automatically make it part of a working adult’s routine. Long days, family responsibilities and unrealistic expectations can all make regular activity difficult. The most useful changes are often small ones that fit existing commitments. Adults may find it easier to become active by adjusting daily habits than by trying to copy a demanding training programme.', 'Nêu đúng đối tượng và hướng giải quyết.'),
        p('Khó khăn','Time is a major barrier. Someone who works all day and then prepares meals or cares for children may have little energy left for a journey to the gym. Cost and distance can add further obstacles. People may also think that exercise only counts if it lasts an hour or involves special equipment. For example, a worker who misses two planned gym sessions may decide that the whole week has been a failure. This all-or-nothing expectation can discourage an activity that could otherwise be continued in a simpler form.', 'Không đổ lỗi chung là lười; phân tích thời gian và kỳ vọng.'),
        p('Thay đổi khả thi','A practical response would be to choose activities that require little preparation. A person could walk for part of the journey to work, take a short walk at lunchtime or do a brief exercise routine at home. Planning a specific time helps: a ten-minute walk after dinner is easier to remember than a general promise to exercise more. Involving family members can also turn activity into shared time rather than a competing responsibility. On a particularly busy day, reducing the length of the activity may be more sustainable than abandoning it completely.', 'Giải pháp khớp trở ngại và có ví dụ lịch cụ thể.'),
        p('Kết luận','In conclusion, work schedules, other responsibilities and overly ambitious plans can prevent adults from exercising regularly. Short, convenient activities and a repeatable schedule can make movement easier to maintain. The aim should be a habit that survives an ordinary busy week, with opportunities to do more when time allows.', 'Không kê đơn y tế; chỉ minh họa lập luận bài thi.')],
    [('family responsibilities','trách nhiệm gia đình'),('a repeatable schedule','lịch có thể duy trì đều'),('all-or-nothing expectation','kỳ vọng hoặc làm trọn vẹn hoặc bỏ hẳn')],
    checks=[c('Khó khăn do công việc','works all day'),c('Khó khăn do kỳ vọng','exercise only counts'),c('Thay đổi trong ngày','walk at lunchtime'),c('Duy trì','reducing the length')]),
]
